isine",[["Nasi gandul","dish/nasi-gandul"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Cucumber","ingredient/cucumber"],["Holy basil","ingredient/holy-basil"],["Krupuk","ingredient/krupuk"],["Mung bean sprout","ingredient/mung-bean-sprout"],["Shrimp paste","ingredient/shrimp-paste"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Seedling","ingredient/seedling"]]}]},"dish/campanile-cake":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/campanile-cake","n":"Campanile (cake)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Corsican cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Campanile, meaning \"the bell tower\", pl. campanili) is a Corsican cake generally shaped like a crown, made of yeast dough. It is a typical dessert of the cuisine of Corsica and is a traditional Easter cake: the boiled eggs in the cake look like little bells inside the bell tower and represent the renewed fertility of the earth after the end of winter, remembering also the tradition to unleash the bells at Easter, after having tethered them at Good Friday."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-campanile-cake"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campanile_(cake)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Corsican cuisine","cuisine/corsican-cuisine"]]}]},"dish/criterion-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/criterion-restaurant","n":"Criterion Restaurant","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Haute cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The Criterion Restaurant is an opulent restaurant complex facing Piccadilly Circus in the heart of London.  It was built by architect Thomas Verity in Neo-Byzantine style for the partnership Spiers and Pond, which opened it in 1873.  Apart from fine dining facilities it has a bar. It is a Grade II* listed building and is among the most historic and oldest restaurants in the world. In the first Sherlock Holmes story, A Study in Scarlet, Dr. Watson is told of his prospective roommate after he meets a friend at the Criterion."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-criterion-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Criterion_Restaurant"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Haute cuisine","cuisine/haute-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Haute cuisine","links":[["In Situ (restaurant)","dish/in-situ-restaurant"],["Rhodes W1","dish/rhodes-w1"]]}]},"dish/dahi-vada":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dahi-vada","n":"Dahi vada","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dahi vada, Dahi bada or Dahi baaraa (Bhojpuri: 𑂠𑂯𑂲 𑂥𑂰𑂩𑂰code: bh is deprecated ) is a type of chaat (snack) originating from the Indian subcontinent. It is prepared by soaking vadas (fried lentil balls) in thick dahi (curd)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dahi-vada"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dahi_vada"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Dahi (curd)","ingredient/dahi-curd"],["Vada","ingredient/vada"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Swasthi's Recipes","ref":"site/indianhealthyrecipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"indianhealthyrecipes.com","note":"Swasthi Shreekanth's long-running blog of everyday Indian home cooking from across the regions.","url":"https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"Hari Ghotra","ref":"site/harighotra-co-uk","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"harighotra.co.uk","note":"UK-based cook Hari Ghotra's recipe library and videos of home-style Indian dishes.","url":"https://www.harighotra.co.uk/indian-recipes","suggeste